[00:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Me? Obsessed with cars? &gt;&gt; [music] &gt;&gt; Yes. Yes, I am. &gt;&gt; [singing] [music]'

[00:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '&gt;&gt; Welcome back to another behind the build. This time we are doing another EV rehab and I am currently in a 1965'

[00:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Sunbeam Tiger. And this is one of those cars that you don\'t really see out on the road too often, let alone an electric one. I personally have never'

[00:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'seen an electric one and funny enough we had one roll into the shop that needed to be completed. This car has a long kind of story to it, so to speak, but I\'ll sum it up for you rather'

[00:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'quickly. This car started out its life as a rust bucket. It was originally sitting in a field and the whole bottom side was fully rusted out and over time it kept'

[01:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'getting worse and worse and worse. The owner then purchased the vehicle from his father and took it to get restored and it was restored about two or three I think two times at two different shops'

[01:19] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and they had a full they did a full rotisserie on it, replaced the entire bottom side of the car, all the side skirts and the whole nine yards. From there it originally had the original'

[01:31] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'motor put back in it, all gas and he drove it like that for quite some time and then it went to an upgraded V8 and I believe I could be wrong, but I think it went to'

[01:45] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Mustang V8 is what he put into it and had that in that for a number of years and then that motor started having leaks and a number of different issues from there. But'

[01:57] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'his son was going to Colorado School of Mines and they needed a project for the year and they decided to convert a car. So the Sunbeam went to School of Mines'

[02:09] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'as a project for students, which was awesome. I think that is a great idea and this car was there for I believe a year or so, maybe less, for their full project and they actually got it all'

[02:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'together, they got it running and then they had a issue with the battery pack. I don\'t recall what the exact issue is, but whenever we got to look at the original batteries that were outside the'

[02:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'car, they were unbalanced. I don\'t know if that was just from them sitting for a long time since or what really happened, but they never really got it on the road fully due to an issue with the battery'

[02:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'pack. So once it was done at School of Mines, it then went to another shop here in Colorado that we actually do a lot of consulting for and so they gave us a call, we came in'

[03:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and checked it out. We\'re we\'re having we\'re having gimbal issues over here. But they gave us a call, we went in, checked it out and pretty much had them just strip it'

[03:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'all down because for many of you know, whoever\'s tried to work on a car that was built by many other people, you never really know what wire goes where, you know, how the wires were done and anything else. So'

[03:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'purely from just a safety standpoint making sure everything is done correctly it is a lot faster to pull all the wires out and just rewire it than it is to trace down every single wire, see where'

[03:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'it goes A to B, make sure the integrity of the wire is good and pretty much the all the details. So it\'s just a lot faster to purely tear it all out. So they started stripping'

[03:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'everything out of the car and decided to go with different batteries. So they opted to go with Tesla modules now to give the owner a bit more range and just kind of rebuild the entire car. So they'

[04:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'had the car for about I think a year, maybe two years that they had the car and they were doing a number of things on it. Hold on, more gimbal issues. You might'

[04:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'just have to hold it over here. You can just put your hand on that side. Don\'t know what\'s happening with our gimbal, but we\'re having issues. Anyways, we they gave them uh designs for high'

[04:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'voltage and low voltage designs so they could build out the whole car and hook it all up. And unfortunately they were not able to finish the vehicle. They got everything stripped out of it and then'

[04:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'didn\'t really get past that point to get it finished. So from there we had it shipped over to our shop and it was pretty much all the way stripped down at that point. They'

[04:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'did a few things as they bought new battery boxes for it and the battery boxes are actually for a Volkswagen bug, but they fit. So they bought those back boxes, incorporated'

[05:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'those into the car, got those mounted and had most of the wiring stripped out by that point. So from there we started building everything out. So we built out the front and rear battery'

[05:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'boxes, made sure the mounts were secure, started running our high voltage, low voltage and really kind of just putting the rest of this car together while also double checking, hey, is the motor mounted properly and safely? Are the'

[05:34] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'battery boxes secure? Kind of all the details that you really want to go over and make make sure they\'re safe with the components that we had and we also changed a few things. So the owner originally had one display'

[05:47] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that they put in the dash over here at the school and then they also put a display in here for the BMS. The BMS that was originally in the car we decided to go with a different one as we'

[06:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'had a different preference there. So we mounted a new screen into the same location as that one. So that one has all the info and everything like that. But before we go out and kind of show you around everything that is done on'

[06:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'this build, I\'ll give you a bit of a tour of the inside. So just like a normal car, you have your ignition, your gauges, so your speed gauge. You also have a digital speed gauge over'

[06:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'here and this is really the gauge for the motor. And then coming over here you have all your analog switches. So these are your lights. This middle one is actually your regen. So all the way up is regen high then you have regen low'

[06:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and you have regen off. So then if the owner likes, he can drive it with low or high and then we also have our wipers of course and then our shift knob. So this car actually has a single speed gearbox'

[06:51] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'in it. So it\'s a Hyper 9 motor and they originally planned on doing a manual gearbox and then somewhere in the design process they decided to go with a single speed gearbox. So this has a Torque'

[07:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Trends single speed gearbox in it. It\'s a great gearbox. It\'s just a little bit louder than going with a manual and then of course there\'s no shifting, which is wonderful, but you don\'t have as broad of a driveability'

[07:17] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'range as far as acceleration goes down low or top speed just because you don\'t have all those gears. But nonetheless it is a great gearbox to have. It makes this car very nice and very easy to'

[07:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'drive, especially for different family members who don\'t know how to drive stick. So that\'s one really nice feature about this car. Going back to the dash with of course our shift knob, just drive in reverse as you would normally expect and then over'

[07:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'here is our display for the BMS. It\'s a bit hard to see because the sun\'s on it. But it just lets you know your state of charge, temperature, voltage, you know, your current, all the general info you could ever need'

[07:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'to monitor your batteries. And if there\'s ever an error or anything else, that will show you all of that information. And then everything else on the inside of the car is all original. So the dash'

[08:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'was redesigned a bit to incorporate these, but everything else on this car is original when it comes to, you know, the seats, the carpeting and everything else that was done to it. The one'

[08:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'difference is just our shift lock right here. So this is off and then when I pull it back this will now engage the lock in the single speed gearbox and pretty much puts a pin in it. So it acts'

[08:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'as putting the car in park. So then you don\'t have to worry about parking on any of the crazy steep hills that proved to be an issue here in Colorado. Now we can hop out of this. I can grab this from Cameron so Cameron can get on'

[08:49] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'out of here. Let\'s see.'

[09:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'All right. Sorry for that short technical difficulty. For some reason the gimbal did not like driving in the car. But it is a beautiful Sunbeam and again'

[09:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'looking at the date codes and everything on this car, it looks to be about a late \'64 or an early \'65'

[09:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'for manufacturing date. And I really wish they built these cars a lot longer, but this is a original Sunbeam Tiger. Whenever the owner had it restored, he'

[09:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'had a few things added such like these side vents and a couple other small details but all in all, it is just a beautiful car. The restoration work um looks great'

[10:00] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'on it along with the paint. I\'m not sure when it was painted, but it still looks fantastic. And one of my favorite features on this car is actually the Minilite wheels. The OG made in England'

[10:13] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Minilites, which is absolutely awesome. Um great racing wheels and just so much so much history to these wheels. But yeah, from the outside you can\'t'

[10:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'even tell this thing is electric. It is a beautiful car. I\'ll have Cameron come over here and we\'ll start in the front. We can go through kind of what\'s in the front of the car and then we\'ll work our way to the back.'

[10:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'You just want to pull the lever, I\'ll open up the front here. And then there we go. Get that in there. Fantastic.'

[10:52] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'So, I\'ll hand this over to Cameron. So, here in the front they opted to change over to Tesla modules. So, if you come over here, you\'ll actually notice this is a front battery box for a'

[11:04] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Volkswagen bug that they incorporated in here and it fits quite perfectly, which is kind of hilarious. But this mod box right here has three Tesla modules in it in the'

[11:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'front along with three more in the rear. So, it\'s running a high-voltage Hyper 9 that puts out 125 horsepower, 175 foot pounds of torque paired to that'

[11:30] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'TorqueTrends single-speed gearbox that we were discussing earlier. And then of course the drive shaft. But up in the front, it\'s pretty simple. It\'s mainly just the box. We have our little booster here. This is a vacuum booster that they'

[11:43] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'originally installed in it and kind of kept all that stuff the same and original. Coming over here, we have our coolant reservoir. Um the inverter on this is'

[11:55] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'cooled and everything for the Hyper 9. Plus our bleeder our br- breather for the TorqueTrends gearbox. Um but yeah, in the front end here, it is very simple.'

[12:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Very clean when it comes to all the electronics. All the electronics for the BMS, the fusing and everything else is mounted up behind underneath the dash in the car. So then out of sight, out of mind. If you ever need to change a fuse'

[12:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'cuz it blows, you can just crawl under there, pull it out and pop a new one in just like you would a modern car. Here in the back, there\'s a bit more going on. So, this is the rear battery box.'

[12:33] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'This is also out of a Volkswagen bug. So, this is a Volkswagen bug box with three more Tesla modules in it here. And then you have your high-voltage shutoff on the side. So, if you ever need to,'

[12:46] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you can shut off high voltage here, your low-voltage connector, and then down in this corner, you\'ll notice we have a Elcon DC to DC along with our 12-V anti-gravity battery. Uh one thing that'

[12:59] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'we always love adding are these anti-gravity batteries. One, they\'re lithium and they last a very long time. But my favorite feature about it is some of these cars don\'t get driven that often. So, the Sunbeam in particular is'

[13:12] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'kind of going to be a weekend warrior when the weather\'s nice. And here in Colorado, we have of course a winter snow season and many of these cars don\'t get driven throughout the whole winter. So, they sit. And well, no matter how'

[13:25] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'low um those batteries will usually go bad. You know, car normal 12-V car batteries have a hard time just sitting for that long for 6 months during the winter and not getting driven. So, we like adding these anti-gravity batteries'

[13:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'because they have a smart BMS in them and when the voltage gets low, they will completely shut off. And so then the battery is still healthy, still good. And all you do is you come in, you press'

[13:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the restart button and you can turn the vehicle back on and you\'re up and running and you\'re good to go and you don\'t have to worry about replacing your battery because it sat for way too long during the winter and everything else.'

[14:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'On this side, um we have a standard high-voltage junction box. This is actually the same kind of box that you would find um in your generic, you know, kits that you would buy for a'

[14:15] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Volkswagen. Um so whenever the other shop got this in, it seems like they pretty much purchased all the parts for a Volkswagen to put it all back together. Uh which actually works great for this car. It\'s not exactly the'

[14:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'design um we would have gone with, but it works really well and it really fits with the owner needs and wants for this vehicle. So, this is your standard um plastic casing. It\'s watertight. And then inside'

[14:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'that is your high-voltage junction box. So, you have all your fuses, your contactors, your precharge and the whole nine yards that you need to run this system. Um here hidden behind this box is actually the charger.'

[14:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'So, you\'ll see right down there, there is the charger for the batteries. And that charges everything up. It does level one and level two. And if I remember correctly, this car charges from empty to full in about 7 to 8'

[15:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'hours. I\'ll have to double-check the math on that one. Um so a good, you know, overnight charge vehicle. And then right here is our J1772 charge port.'

[15:20] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'So, you can use any standard charging um at home or in public to get this guy charged up. I\'ll close this back here. But whenever it comes to'

[15:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'range on this car, due to the single-speed gearbox, uh you top out at about 70 I think it\'s'

[15:44] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: '70-75 mph uh is what you top out at as the, you know, we\'re pretty much limited by the gearing and the RPM that the motor can spin at equals your top speed. And it\'s about 70-75. It\'s not 100%'

[15:56] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'spot on with RPMs to top speed. And other than that, range-wise, I don\'t know. What\'s going on? Yeah, we got to fix this thing. Um but range-wise on this car, it comes out to be a lot'

[16:11] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'farther than you expect purely due to the fact that most of the driving that you do is around-town driving in the range of, you know, 40 to 60 mph. And so'

[16:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'you get a huge range advantage on it instead of cruising at high highway speeds. We\'re not certain of the exact range on this one yet. Um it\'s we\'ve estimated about 130 to 150, but we'

[16:36] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'haven\'t fully run it completely dry yet to be for certain that\'s what we get on average based off of all different driving styles. Uh but that is the closest estimate that we\'ve had so far'

[16:48] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'for range on this car. And it\'s been a great car to drive. We really enjoy it. I can close this back down. We\'ll hop in. We\'ll show you what it\'s like to drive this thing.'

[17:01] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Um and it\'s just really uh a joy to drive. It\'s such a beautiful car, especially on a day like like this being a convertible. You just you really can\'t go wrong with this thing.'

[17:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Here, we\'ll hop on in here. And if you still have your soft top back here. So, if in doubt, the sun\'s too much or it rains, you can pop that guy right up. And that is still in wonderful'

[17:26] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'condition. So, get in here. I can hold this for Cameron so he can get a seatbelt on. And I will do the same. There you go. All right. So,'

[17:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the car is currently on. I will turn you off turn it off. And I will walk you through kind of how it works. So, you hopped in the car. I\'m just going to turn my key on.'

[17:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'You\'ll see the BMS come on. It will show a precharge doing this precharge for the system. It\'ll then go to drive. And then you know the vehicle is good to drive. From there, you want to make sure that'

[18:02] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'your parking lock is off. So then the gearbox can spin. And you have your shifter, so you put your foot on the brake. We\'ll shift it into drive. And then just like a normal automatic, you will just press the gas'

[18:14] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'and go. And then we will our off. And you can hear it a bit more. I\'ll kind of get on it a little bit so you can hear it.'

[18:27] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'Sorry for making you dizzy on this one. Apparently uh our gimbal is not happy today. So, right now we have the regen all the'

[18:40] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'way up. Uh purely it\'s just how how we like driving since we\'re so used [music] to driving these EVs is we just keep the regen high, um which is really nice. But this car'

[18:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'drives great. It\'s super quiet. It handles wonderful. You can hear a bit of a whine from the motor until about 30-40 and then it goes away. Not sure if you\'re able to'

[19:08] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'hear that at all, but this is just a blast to drive. Uh we hate to see this one go. Thankfully, it is here local in Colorado. So, we\'re able to see this car at local car meets and'

[19:23] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'everything else. So, it would be great to have this car here local. But yeah, that is everything on the 1965 Sunbeam Tiger'

[19:35] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'EV conversion. So, stay tuned for our next behind the build.'
